\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"735b56c4f7fcb34320a7d6d5ca6d9b68b2b43076e24d046815a067720ccfcf83","event_uuid":"847a2aed-ead8-479f-b4fa-6c00c4cf5075","position":{"commit_sha":"fdcfca9b863f225aaaa3bffc2761df3316344cd3","position":"1787461520467957001-847a2aed-ead8-479f-b4fa-6c00c4cf5075"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"82026b48b251c2a0ef1499ad5df30149ca203b81430653f091ce77327b9ced55","event_uuid":"15a4d998-ec5f-4cef-8580-f39be5fb0c2e","position":{"commit_sha":"cf9214a10b51b6bd42b457977f0e93d242b4a2ec","position":"1787462520097258001-15a4d998-ec5f-4cef-8580-f39be5fb0c2e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation for blocking finding fe026a21741d96d81: clarified that existing gen_cli_help rendering applies the version-stable usage/metavar normalization contract, both public help entry points serve the exact same committed bytes, and raw argparse fallthrough ends only for registry-declared top-level help owners. Also replaced the representative-route test with registry-driven coverage of all visible canonical intercept routes. Scope remains the ADR 0100 help-discovery slice; no new router, parser, help source, or writing-policy enforcement was added.","timestamp":1787418428121660001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation for findings f7933b1b934bcd188, faa324f55e688c487, f6ce8b8cd4fedff2e, f580040ac6aec2172, and f64cc306b459cc6c2: named the concrete helper move into gen_cli_help, removed the independent reference renderer in favor of committed-byte consumption, enumerated the runtime/generator census seams, pinned the exact no-new-metadata ownership predicate, preserved nested argparse fallthrough, and reconciled the two existing overview exemptions. Acceptance checks were split and now cover the preserved branch. The operator-approved rejection of mechanical writing enforcement and the Markdown-only reduced test policy remains explicit and unchanged.","timestamp":1787419173255642001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third plan-review remediation for findings f81010e3af4b0c56f, f3b23ede1a6113c69, f7b491a6d405c9916, and f4d3c72907ada4387: enumerated both test consumers, mirrored the routable census, added the four missing route-owned parser summaries, and preserved trusted-env explicit multiline usage by gating `_unwrap_usage` on `parser.usage is None`. Also named the existing 3.11/3.12/3.13 matrix proof, retained the formatter-contract exception, split compound acceptance checks, and kept the no-mechanical-writing-enforcement and Markdown-only reduced-test policies unchanged.","timestamp":1787420142112964001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fourth plan-review remediation for finding fe646dc4830c0e337 and advisory fb2c90d4aae439718: expanded `_NESTED_INTERCEPTS` to the full import-safe set `audit`, `identity`, `llm`, `prompt`, `criteria`, `workflow`; added the fourth inlined help-backed census site; and made the parser-introspective contract test prove runtime membership plus child-help fallthrough. Tightened acceptance criteria below the oversize threshold while retaining the rejection of mechanical writing enforcement and the unchanged Markdown-only reduced test policy.","timestamp":1787420929405321001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution preflight found that the remediated plan named parser factories, the CLI reference generator, generated route artifacts, and contract tests that were absent from the recorded file impact. Replaced the seven-path declaration with the complete 35-path planned edit set and expanded verification to cover both generators, focused unit contracts, public help parity, nested-family no-write behavior, formatter scope, lint, and type checking. This material correction intentionally invalidates the earlier attestation. A fresh plan review is required before claim.","timestamp":1787423237257475001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fifth plan-review remediation for blocking finding f81034227578a46fd: added `config` to the exact `_NESTED_INTERCEPTS` set; documented that `config validate` is a handler-dispatched pseudo-subcommand with no populated argparse `_SubParsersAction` and therefore cannot be discovered by parser introspection; and added an explicit `rebar config validate --help` plan and acceptance check proving control reaches `build_validate` and returns validate child help instead of top-level config help. The 35-path material scope remains unchanged, as do the explicit rejection of mechanical writing enforcement and the Markdown-only reduced test policy.","timestamp":1787425476909871001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution scope audit found two omitted behavior contracts, identity child parsers without help actions, and stale comments that would become inaccurate after committed artifacts expand. The description now names the child-help mechanism, public generator coverage, held-out all-route oracle, and comment corrections. File impact now covers 46 paths, including `test_plan_review_gate.py`, `test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py`, `verify_commit.py`, `verify_authorship.py`, and `_llm_commands.py`. The five verify commands now include every edited contract test. This material correction requires a fresh normal plan review before code edits.","timestamp":1787455719969477001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fresh normal plan review passed with a signed attestation at `1a2b59ea91`. The review ran the LLM tier and reported no blocking findings. Advisory `f35f97d8337178085` is accepted in scope. Generator tests will prove identical bytes under distinct `COLUMNS` values, and generation will use a fixed width. Advisory `fb59727dfac76fbbf` does not warrant decomposition because 21 paths are generated artifacts and the remaining edits implement or document one help-ownership invariant. Advisory `f607dd457c67f9209` does not identify an ambiguous behavior contract, so the signed plan remains unchanged.","timestamp":1787457354160860001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out TDD contract card. ADR 0100 sections 3 through 5 require fixed-width committed help bytes, pre-operation serving, and handler-owned nested help. Preconditions were confirmed. Twenty-one visible intercept routes lack artifacts, identity child parsers reject `--help`, and runtime nested ownership omits five parser-backed families. The production paths are the public generator entry point, in-process CLI dispatch, and CLI subprocesses. Exact postconditions are committed-byte equality, zero operation-path calls, zero repository state, successful child usage, cross-width equality, and preserved trusted-env usage lines. Focused RED produced six visible failures and eight held-out failures for those reasons. The existing `config validate --help` child-parser contract passed as the control. The held-out source is outside the worktree at `/Users/joeoakhart/f12-heldout-oracle/oracle.py`.","timestamp":1787458191709340001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution scope reconciliation added `src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py`. Its existing comment stated that `audit` owned top-level help. F12 makes the registry-backed committed artifact authoritative for top-level help, so leaving the comment unchanged would make developer documentation inaccurate. The implementation corrects that comment without changing audit behavior. The added path is within the approved goal of correcting stale ownership comments. This material scope update invalidates the prior plan attestation. A fresh normal plan review will run before validation and commit.","timestamp":1787460064068590001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The fresh normal plan review passed with a signed attestation at `dc2f809896`. It reported no blocking or indeterminate findings. Advisory `fb59727dfac76fbbf` remains accepted because 21 paths are generated artifacts and the remaining edits express one help-ownership invariant. Advisory `f607dd457c67f9209` remains accepted because the focused verification commands map each criterion to observable behavior despite grammatical conjunctions. Dropped low-validity finding `fc2509af46aa44ad7` does not require a scope change. The held-out oracle covers identity child help without repository state, and the focused contracts preserve the approved distinction between top-level committed help and nested parser ownership.","timestamp":1787461520467957001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution validation is complete at `dc2f809896`. Both generator drift checks pass. D3 passes with 36 tests. D4 passes with 221 tests. The restored held-out oracle passes all nine cases. Its cross-width case previously failed under a seeded removal of fixed-width generation and returned to green after restoration. `make lint` passes. `make typecheck` passes across 639 source files after a typed cast preserved the fixed-width formatter binding. `git diff --check` passes. The worktree contains exactly 47 changed paths, matching file impact, and no changed `src/rebar` module exceeds 800 lines. The implementation required four TDD attempts. Per operator direction, the unrelated full suite was not run. Manual writing review identified inherited parser prose outside the approved F12 scope. Proposed remediation is recorded as `alamode-greasy-jerboa` and linked through `discovered_from`.","timestamp":1787462520097258001}],"created_at":1787417227306077001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0cf6daca-46bb-4e7d-a664-42d7ae8d9ef8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3d23-26af-bc3f-476c"}],"description":"## Context\nADR 0100 makes the immutable route registry and parser factories authoritative for command identity, grammar, and committed help. Twenty-one visible pure-intercept routes support `rebar <command> --help` but remain absent from overview help and fail under `rebar help <command>`. The `identity` child parsers disable their own help actions, so `rebar identity create --help` reaches top-level usage and exits with an error.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the help-backed predicate exactly `not route.hidden and not route.retired` in `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py`, and `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py`. Do not add route metadata.\n- Add nonblank parser descriptions to `reconcile.build`, `enrich.build`, `identity.build`, and `certs.build_trusted_env` so route-owned summaries populate overview help.\n- Move `_unwrap_usage` and `_collapse_metavars` from `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` into `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`. Apply usage unwrapping only to intercept routes without explicit parser usage. Apply metavar normalization to intercept option lines before byte normalization. Preserve the explicit multiline `trusted-env` usage.\n- Expand the generator census through its public entry point. Do not test the private `_expected` helper. Generate one committed artifact for each newly help-backed route and regenerate `overview.txt`.\n- Widen top-level help pre-scan to every live visible route. Keep `_NESTED_INTERCEPTS` exactly `audit`, `config`, `identity`, `llm`, `prompt`, `criteria`, and `workflow` so nonleading child help reaches the owning parser or handler.\n- Enable help on the `identity create`, `identity use`, and `identity key` child parsers. Prove that each child returns child usage and exits successfully.\n- Keep the explicit `config validate --help` contract because `config validate` is handler-dispatched and has no populated argparse subparser action.\n- Keep parser-introspective nested-family coverage for argparse-backed families. Assert that the derived family set matches runtime ownership, then exercise each child-help path. Keep the 42-subprocess all-route contract in the held-out outer oracle.\n- Delete `_render_intercept` from `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`. Make CLI reference generation consume `subcommand_help(route.name)` for every documented route. Update the two legacy expectations in `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n- Correct comments and docstrings that claim intercept routes lack committed help. The affected paths include `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_workflow_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/verify_commit.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py`, `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6.py`, and `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`.\n- Update affected expectations in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py` and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py`.\n- Retain `_OVERVIEW_OMIT` as exactly `bridge-fsck` and `bridge-probe`. Retain the test allowlist as exactly `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`.\n- Keep `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py` scoped away from pure-intercept parsers because generator normalization permits those parsers to retain the standard library formatter.\n- Regenerate package help and the CLI reference through their existing generators. The Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13 CI cells must pass the help drift check against the same committed bytes.\n- Do not add another router, parser, help source, mechanical writing-policy gate, or change to the Markdown-only reduced test policy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every live visible route outside the documented omit set appears exactly once in overview help.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` succeeds for every canonical pure-intercept route returned by the registry.\n- [ ] The pure-intercept help contract proves that no command handler executes.\n- [ ] The pure-intercept help contract proves that no ticket store is mounted or created.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` returns the matching committed artifact bytes.\n- [ ] Top-level `rebar <command> --help` returns the matching committed artifact bytes.\n- [ ] Every pure-intercept parser factory supplies a nonblank overview description.\n- [ ] The committed `trusted-env` usage banner preserves separate `add` and `revoke` lines.\n- [ ] Each CLI-reference pure-intercept syntax block equals the matching committed artifact.\n- [ ] A repository-wide semantic and string search reports zero `_render_intercept` references.\n- [ ] All four help-backed census sites use the live-visible predicate.\n- [ ] The exact overview exemptions remain `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`.\n- [ ] Hidden aliases and retired spellings remain absent from overview discovery.\n- [ ] `_NESTED_INTERCEPTS` equals `audit`, `config`, `identity`, `llm`, `prompt`, `criteria`, and `workflow`.\n- [ ] Every parser-introspectable nested family returns child-parser usage for each child.\n- [ ] `rebar identity create --help`, `rebar identity use --help`, and `rebar identity key --help` return their child usage and exit successfully.\n- [ ] `rebar config validate --help` reaches `build_validate` and returns validate child help.\n- [ ] Comments and test docstrings describe committed help ownership accurately.\n- [ ] The help drift check passes on supported Python versions.\n- [ ] The CLI-reference drift check passes.\n- [ ] No competing routing, parser, or help mechanism is introduced.\n- [ ] No mechanical writing enforcement is introduced.\n- [ ] The Markdown-only reduced test policy remains unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_help.py","reason":"Generate committed help for every live visible route and normalize intercept usage."},{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Consume committed help for every documented route and remove the separate intercept renderer."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py","reason":"Serve committed help for visible intercept routes while preserving nested-family ownership."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"Correct top-level help ownership guidance after pre-scan expands."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"Correct committed-help ownership comments for LLM-backed commands."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"Correct nested-help ownership comments for LLM evaluation commands."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_workflow_commands.py","reason":"Correct nested-help ownership comments for workflow commands."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","reason":"Correct top-level help ownership documentation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_commit.py","reason":"Correct the stale claim that the route lacks a committed help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py","reason":"Correct the stale claim that the route lacks a committed help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py","reason":"Provide the route-owned overview description."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/enrich.py","reason":"Provide the route-owned overview description."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/identity.py","reason":"Provide the overview description and enable help on identity child parsers."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py","reason":"Provide the trusted-env route-owned overview description."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"Regenerate the complete top-level command overview."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/workflow.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-identity.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-completion.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-commit-ticket.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-authorship.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/sign-review.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/scan-spec.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/review-code.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/remote-cert.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/reconcile.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/prompt.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/llm.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/jira-onboard.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/identity.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/explain.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/enrich.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/criteria.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/config.txt","reason":"Add the generated committed help artifact for this route."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerate command syntax from committed help artifacts."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py","reason":"Pin complete help generation, summaries, and explicit usage handling."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Pin committed-help consumption and correct stale documentation."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"Use the live-visible route census and correct stale documentation."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py","reason":"Pin nested-family fallthrough and no-write behavior under the widened census."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py","reason":"Align formatter-scope guidance with generator normalization."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py","reason":"Correct help ownership guidance in the mount-gate contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6.py","reason":"Correct help ownership guidance in the registry cutover contract."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py","reason":"Update help expectations affected by the widened committed-help census."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py","reason":"Update the held-out all-route help contract for committed artifacts."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py","reason":"Correct the stale claim that audit owns top-level help after committed help expands."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f7e4-4d33-f231-4774"],["relates_to","3d23-26af-bc3f-476c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","parent_status_uuid":"32b9d93f-78b4-497d-94cf-0c9f34e91d8d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["documentation","f12","cli"],"ticket_id":"65c9-aba3-c744-483a","ticket_type":"story","title":"F12 complete ADR 0100 CLI command discovery","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Committed CLI help is current"},{"command":"python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"Generated CLI reference is current"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6.py -q","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"Focused help generators and registry contracts preserve committed-artifact behavior"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q","dd_id":"D4","dd_text":"Public help, nested ownership, no-write behavior, and affected lifecycle contracts pass"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"D5","dd_text":"Source lint and type checks pass"}]},"source_event_uuids":["32b9d93f-78b4-497d-94cf-0c9f34e91d8d","3e32ac22-9689-4837-8f3e-c5d1c0dba081","263a1e7a-8794-4df8-b508-ba7f190c7805","304d21dc-3b23-4b73-a438-6bf3bd3c8917","6bc6208a-37df-4cec-afa3-d1a398a20e8a","b566bb1b-d07d-457a-ba88-9becab3b7377","21207b2c-b2d8-44f4-bddb-7480242842e1","459aea1f-8947-4e97-984f-4658c4ae920a","0cf6daca-46bb-4e7d-a664-42d7ae8d9ef8","b8102f9c-3218-4610-94a7-c44da2c4da92","18b19fd3-c343-47f7-bfad-5595674e84f8","eed771ad-21b3-4c6b-b698-8499383fa919","94788124-96b2-41e9-a379-d7df5153e9d8","847a2aed-ead8-479f-b4fa-6c00c4cf5075","15a4d998-ec5f-4cef-8580-f39be5fb0c2e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787462520097258002,"uuid":"c98fa725-9cff-437d-b2f7-ff87a6e912a2"}